factcheck by anthropic/claude-haiku-5-5: 6 problems
  The reel_script says Govindasamy died at Salem Government Medical College hospital on November 17; the article says he collapsed on Tuesday Nov 17 and was taken to Erode GH first, then died at Salem. The date is not explicitly stated as the death date, which is roughly consistent, but the reel_script omits that he collapsed at a public toilet and was first treated at Erode.
  The reel_script states the protest was on November 18 (நவம்பர் 18ஆம் தேதி); the article only says Wednesday, with no explicit date given, so the date is an invented detail.
  The reel_script and caption say the procession went to the cemetery (மயானம்); the article says the protesters went from there to the மயானம், which matches, but the caption's line 'உடலுடன் மயானத்துக்குச் சென்றனர்' is fine; however the reel_script says the body was 'கூறாய்வு செய்ய' after which it was brought, which is consistent.
  The reel_script says 'மாலையில்தான் அனுமதி கடிதம் வழங்கப்பட்டது' and then 'இதனால் செவ்வாய்க்கிழமை கூறாய்வு செய்ய முடியாமல் போனது', which mixes the sequence: the article says the post-mortem could not be done on Tuesday because of the delay, which is consistent, but the reel_script omits that the sub-inspector allegedly delayed the process and said the deceased's family was insulted; only partially covered.
  The slides_spec 'லிருந்து' line 'சிவகிரி காவல் உதவி ஆய்வாளர் முருகேசன்' is a grammatically broken/unclear Tamil sentence (a name with no verb in a bullet framed as a reason), and the second slide mixes the sub-inspector's name into a line about why the protest happened.
  The reel_script's 'உதவி ஆய்வாளர் மீது நடவடிக்கை எடுப்பதாக உறுதி அளிக்கப்பட்டது' correctly reports the assurance, but the caption and reel_script both say the sub-inspector was named Murugesan only in one place, while the slide 'ஏன் போராட்டம்' line merges the insult allegation with the officer's name into one line, mixing two facts.
